  "dom_id": "step-q104982",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Let $A$ and $B$ be the set of all non-negative integer powers of $2$ and the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0,$ respectively. What is $A\\cap B?$",
  "worked_solution": "The powers of $2$ that are greater or equal to $1$ are\n\n$$\nA=\\{1,2,4,8,16,32,64,…\\}.\n$$\n\nMultiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB=\\{4,8,12,16,20,24,…\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $A\\cap B$ is the *intersection* of $A$ and $B,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in *both* $A$ and $B.$  In other words, $A\\cap B$ denotes the set of natural numbers that are both powers of $2$ and multiples of $4.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cap B & =\\{1,2,4,8,16,32,64,…\\}\\cap \\{4,8,12,16,20,24,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{4,8,16,32,64,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
